{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze the task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01: Implement `api_call_loss_filter` through `solve(case)`.\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. For each call, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n2. Normalize gain by prediction_tokens (normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens)\n3. A call is accepted if: parseable == True AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Return accepted_call_ids (in source order) and diagnostics (in source order)\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- threshold = 0.05\n- call0: loss_without=1.94835097, loss_with=0.38569502, tokens=5, parseable=True\n  - gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595\n  - normalized_gain = 1.56265595 / 5 = 0.31253119\n  - accepted: True (parseable=True, normalized_gain \u003e= 0.05)\n\n- call1: loss_without=1.06116273, loss_with=0.68319969, tokens=4, parseable=True\n  - gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304\n  - normalized_gain = 0.37796304 / 4 = 0.09449076\n  - accepted: True\n\n- call2: loss_without=1.21810502, loss_with=0.47260371, tokens=6, parseable=True\n  - gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131\n  - normalized_gain = 0.74550131 / 6 = 0.12425022\n  - accepted: True\n\n- call3: loss_without=1.05721833, loss_with=0.29767903, tokens=5, parseable=True\n  - gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393\n  - normalized_gain = 0.7595393 / 5 = 0.1519078 (wait, let me recalculate: 0.7595393/5 = 0.15190786)\n  - accepted: True\n\n- call4: loss_without=1.06717367, loss_with=0.85733566, tokens=5, parseable=True\n  - gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801\n  - normalized_gain = 0.20983801 / 5 = 0.041967602\n  - accepted: False (normalized_gain \u003c 0.05)\n\n- call5: loss_without=1.66191711, loss_with=0.89798497, tokens=4, parseable=True\n  - gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214\n  - normalized_gain = 0.76393214 / 4 = 0.190983035\n  - accepted: True\n\nSo accepted_call_ids = [\"call0\", \"call1\", \"call2\", \"call3\", \"call5\"]\n\nNow let me check fixture case-002:\n- call4: parseable=False → not accepted regardless of gain\n\nThe implementation looks straightforward. I need to:\n1. Validate required fields\n2. Compute normalized_gain for each call\n3. Accept if parseable AND normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n4. Return in source order\n\nThe candidate artifact mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I should round normalized_gain. The schema says `\"type\": \"number\"` for normalized_gain. I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places. Let me think... the artifact doesn't specify the rounding precision. I'll use Python's `round()` with maybe 8 decimal places or just return the float as-is. Actually \"rounded\" might mean a specific precision. Let me not over-interpret and just return the float value.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the schema - it just says `\"type\": \"number\"`. The artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify precision. I'll round to, say, 10 significant digits or just return the raw float.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be a number\")\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. The output must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me format this properly as JSON.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    required_call_fields = {\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"}\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        missing = required_call_fields - set(call.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Call missing required fields: {missing}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be at least 1 for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01QmTgz6W953dKMWZ2lgn9Ew","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2504,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":15,"output_tokens":1773,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1345},"service_tier":"standard"}}